  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "With the new age verification update added with features such as limiting certain instances and groups to only 18+ verified members, I feel like there should also be an option for those under 18 to do the same for users their age as well; it'd be a fair addition to those under the age of 18 who understand their limitations when hanging around more mature people.\n\nOften times in group instances specifically for teenage users under the age of 18, many adults hang around minors, occasionally in an explicit manner with no way of being prohibited aside from the chance of being caught by a mod (they can't be everywhere, y'know). Even if they aren't, it can feel uncomfortable to some teen users trying to enjoy their time with others their age.\n\nTo emphasize, this should only be a feature to those that are VERIFIED to be under the age of 18. That way, a safer environment can be ensured for younger users. \n\nWhile some might be concerned that this could be a dangerous opportunity for dangerous adult individuals to interact with children, the current features that verify identity within the third party company responsible for verifying users' age currently such as a quick facial recognition scan can certainly pose as an effective barrier to prevent this sort of thing. If one were to go through the effort to bypass all the security barriers, then the concern could be vise-versa (A minor finding a way to verify themselves as 18+ in order to join mature instances). In addition, a \"verified\" symbol could potentially only be visible to other verified users under the age of 18 if that does become a concern. However, it could pose as a warning to those above the age of 18 the same way the feature currently does for minors when viewing an 18+ verified profile.",
